1
00:00:00,623 --> 00:00:04,533
Every day, students walk past broken things on campus.

2
00:00:04,583 --> 00:00:05,753
Wi-Fi that drops,

3
00:00:05,803 --> 00:00:07,473
heaters that die,

4
00:00:07,523 --> 00:00:08,433
railings that wobble.

5
00:00:09,518 --> 00:00:12,028
Reporting means finding the right office,

6
00:00:12,078 --> 00:00:13,128
filling out a form,

7
00:00:13,178 --> 00:00:14,868
and never hearing back.

8
00:00:14,918 --> 00:00:16,808
So most problems just go unreported.

9
00:00:17,209 --> 00:00:20,059
We are three freshmen from WPI.

10
00:00:20,109 --> 00:00:21,609
My name is Nicolas Nabhan.

11
00:00:21,659 --> 00:00:22,709
I'm Guillermo Guerra.

12
00:00:22,759 --> 00:00:25,609
And I'm Vladislav Hushcha.

13
00:00:26,022 --> 00:00:30,772
We built UniFix for the Hackachusetts Civic Action Challenge V4.

14
00:00:30,822 --> 00:00:32,072
Better college experiences.

15
00:00:32,606 --> 00:00:36,236
Students say what's wrong in plain words and it goes straight to the

16
00:00:36,286 --> 00:00:37,696
one team that can fix it.

17
00:00:39,226 --> 00:00:40,216
Here's the student view.

18
00:00:40,266 --> 00:00:44,836
A quick pop-up tells judges exactly where they are.

19
00:00:45,316 --> 00:00:47,706
The campus feed shows what's open,

20
00:00:47,756 --> 00:00:49,806
what's urgent, what's already fixed.

21
00:00:50,288 --> 00:00:54,838
The live map shows where problems cluster,

22
00:00:54,888 --> 00:00:56,938
colored by severity.

23
00:00:57,420 --> 00:01:00,450
Click any bubble to see every report inside it.

24
00:01:01,980 --> 00:01:04,890
First, quality, then spam,

25
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:06,350
jokes and claims like

26
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,310
“I won a million dollars”

27
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:10,510
are blocked before they reach staff.

28
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:13,390
So every report is a real one in the queue.

29
00:01:14,066 --> 00:01:17,156
But safety beats everything.

30
00:01:17,206 --> 00:01:19,176
Ari reads as you type.

31
00:01:19,656 --> 00:01:23,226
So the moment something sounds like emergency,

32
00:01:23,276 --> 00:01:29,366
UniFix shows Call 911 or campus police before any AI runs.

33
00:01:30,896 --> 00:01:32,806
Now a real report.

34
00:01:32,856 --> 00:01:34,206
Just say what's wrong.

35
00:01:34,687 --> 00:01:36,257
AI picks the team,

36
00:01:36,307 --> 00:01:38,457
then asks only what's missing.

37
00:01:39,987 --> 00:01:41,897
Ari checks the past.

38
00:01:41,947 --> 00:01:43,057
Nine similar reports,

39
00:01:43,107 --> 00:01:45,257
usually fixed in about three days,

40
00:01:45,307 --> 00:01:47,777
plus quick fixes to try first.

41
00:01:48,257 --> 00:01:49,547
Add a photo if you like.

42
00:01:50,572 --> 00:01:53,142
Check the card and post.

43
00:01:53,711 --> 00:01:56,921
It's rated Medium and sent to the IT team.

44
00:01:56,971 --> 00:01:59,161
And only IT staff can see it.

45
00:01:59,211 --> 00:02:01,461
Everyone who co-signs stays in the loop.

46
00:02:01,942 --> 00:02:03,452
On the staff side,

47
00:02:03,502 --> 00:02:06,032
each team sees only its own area,

48
00:02:06,082 --> 00:02:08,312
ranked by severity times

49
00:02:08,362 --> 00:02:10,372
how many students are affected,

50
00:02:10,422 --> 00:02:12,132
not by who complains loudest.

51
00:02:12,613 --> 00:02:14,563
If something's unclear,

52
00:02:14,613 --> 00:02:17,043
staff can message the reporter directly.

53
00:02:18,276 --> 00:02:22,106
They can post public updates,

54
00:02:22,156 --> 00:02:23,726
then mark it solved.

55
00:02:23,776 --> 00:02:27,486
Everyone who co-signs is notified automatically.

56
00:02:27,973 --> 00:02:29,923
The student gets a notification.

57
00:02:29,973 --> 00:02:31,603
One click opens the conversation,

58
00:02:31,653 --> 00:02:33,163
and they answer right there.

59
00:02:33,213 --> 00:02:34,243
No emails, no forms,

60
00:02:34,293 --> 00:02:35,183
no lost tickets.

61
00:02:36,713 --> 00:02:38,983
A misunderstanding becomes a two-minute chat.

62
00:02:40,513 --> 00:02:43,223
We built UniFix with Kiro,

63
00:02:43,273 --> 00:02:44,723
with some specs,

64
00:02:44,773 --> 00:02:47,403
steering, and skills,

65
00:02:47,453 --> 00:02:49,623
backed by over 300 tests.

66
00:02:51,153 --> 00:02:53,323
UniFix works for any Massachusetts campus,

67
00:02:53,373 --> 00:02:54,923
so you can try it yourself.

